$add('USER-003', 'Users', 'Existing database upgraded', 'info', 'The new company, job_title and phone columns are added by database/schema.sql for new installs. An existing database was upgraded with one ALTER TABLE; rows without a company show Not set.');


// ---------- Stage 1: companies
$add('COMP-001', 'Companies', 'Companies section: list, details, add, edit', 'pass', 'companies.php lists companies with search (name, city, KvK, email), sorting and pagination; company.php shows details, users and invoices with the outstanding amount; company_edit.php adds and edits with validation (name, KvK 8 digits, VAT format, email, website) and refuses a duplicate KvK number. Markup in names and notes is escaped, % in a search is literal, hostile sort and page values are handled.');
$add('COMP-002', 'Companies', 'A company with users can not be deleted by accident', 'pass', 'Deleting needs a confirmation page; a company with users is refused both by the page (also for a forged request) and by a database foreign key. Invoices of a deleted company are kept and only lose the link.');
$add('COMP-003', 'Companies', 'Links between users, invoices and companies', 'pass', 'The users list shows the company as a link and filters and searches by it; a user is assigned from their own page; invoice_new.php has a company picker that fills in name, email and address and stores the link; the invoice page links back. A company that does not exist is rejected.');
$add('COMP-004', 'Companies', 'Migration of existing data', 'pass', 'database/migrate.php (run as root, safe to repeat) turned the old users.company text into company rows in a scratch database: one row per distinct name, every user linked, the demo tag kept, the text column dropped, a second run changes nothing. The live database was upgraded with it.');
$add('COMP-005', 'Companies', 'Demo data and removal', 'pass', 'The 14 demo companies are real rows with addresses, KvK and VAT numbers; every demo user and invoice links to one. Removing demo data keeps a company that a real user or kept invoice still uses.');
$add('COMP-006', 'Companies', 'Phone-width layout of the new pages', 'info', 'The new pages reuse the existing scrolling-table and form patterns. The browser tool could not shrink the viewport during this stage, so 360 px was not measured; the full-site crawl at 360 / 768 / 1440 px is still to be run after the last stage.');

// ---------- Stage 2: notes and timeline
$add('NOTE-001', 'Notes', 'Notes and timeline on users and companies', 'pass', 'A form on user.php and company.php adds a note, call, email or meeting; the timeline lists them newest first, and a company timeline also shows invoices issued. The author is always the signed-in account (a forged author field is ignored). Text is escaped and line breaks kept; empty notes, unknown kinds and notes on a missing user or company are refused; a signed-out or token-less request is refused.');
$add('NOTE-002', 'Notes', 'Length cap', 'fixed', 'The automated test expected a 5000-character note to be refused. The global input filter in security.php already cuts every value to 2000 characters before the page sees it, so such a note is saved capped at 2000. The test now asserts the cap.', 'No code change needed; test updated to match the designed behaviour.');
$add('NOTE-003', 'Notes', 'Notes with deleted or demo records', 'pass', 'Deleting a company deletes its notes. Demo data adds notes to every demo company and 20 users; removing demo data deletes them, plus any hand-written note left on a removed demo user or company.');

// ---------- Stage 3: tickets
$add('TCK-001', 'Tickets', 'Create, comment, status flow', 'pass', 'ticket_new.php validates subject, description, priority, company, contact (must belong to the chosen company; a contact alone brings their company) and assignee, and numbers the ticket TCK-0001 and up. Comments store the signed-in account as author. Status moves freely between open, in progress, waiting and resolved; resolving sets the resolved time and reopening clears it; a closed ticket can only be reopened. Every change leaves a line in the thread and in the activity log.');
$add('TCK-002', 'Tickets', 'List: filters, search, sorting, pagination', 'pass', 'Status chips with counts, priority, assignee (including unassigned) and company filters, search on reference, subject and company (a typed % is literal), all seven sort columns both ways, and pagination including a page beyond the end. Hostile sort, array and quote values return a normal page.');
$add('TCK-003', 'Tickets', 'Safe output and access', 'pass', 'Markup in subjects, descriptions and comments is escaped on the ticket, list and company pages. Signed-out requests are redirected; a POST without a CSRF token is 403; a comment on a missing ticket is 404.');
$add('TCK-004', 'Tickets', 'Tickets on company, user and Overview', 'pass', 'Open tickets are listed on company and user pages, the company timeline shows Ticket opened, and the Overview has an Open tickets tile with the urgent count. Deleting a company keeps its tickets; deleting a ticket deletes its comments.');
$add('TCK-005', 'Tickets', 'Test suite itself', 'fixed', 'Adding the ticket tables made the old-database migration test fail because the scratch database could not drop companies while tickets referenced it, and a leftover test user from an aborted run blocked cleanup.', 'The test drops the newer tables first and removes leftover test users before it starts.');

// ---------- Stage 4: global search
$add('SRCH-001', 'Search', 'One search across users, companies, invoices and tickets', 'pass', 'search.php groups results with a count per group and links each row to its page. Users are found by name, email and company; companies by name, city, KvK and email; invoices by number, customer and email; tickets by reference, subject and company. Groups are cut at 8 rows with a View all link to the full list. The top-bar box now sends people there.');
$add('SRCH-002', 'Search', 'Typed characters are searched literally', 'fixed', 'A typed % or _ acted as a wildcard in the invoice list search (and would have in the new one). Found while writing the search tests.', 'LIKE characters are escaped in search.php and in the invoice list.');
$add('SRCH-003', 'Search', 'No results, hostile input, rate limit', 'pass', 'An empty search shows help, an unknown term shows a clear empty state, SQL-looking text, an array parameter and a 500-character query are handled, and the search text is escaped when shown back. search.php is limited to 60 requests a minute per address (then 429).');
$add('SRCH-004', 'Search', 'The two hidden easter eggs still work', 'pass', 'Automated: both buttons and the exact trigger words are still in the page and motion.js, and both pages open. In the browser: "creator" and "CREATOR " show the creator button, "creators" shows nothing, "Teletollie" shows the dictionary button, "teletollie" shows nothing. The first browser attempt showed nothing only because the deferred script had not loaded yet.');


// ---------- Stage 5: CSV export and import
$add('CSV-001', 'Export and import', 'Export users, companies, invoices and tickets', 'pass', 'export.php?type= downloads each list as UTF-8 CSV with a byte-order mark (Excel reads it correctly), named type-DATE.csv, not cached. Money is plain euros. Quotes, semicolons and line breaks inside cells survive. Every export is logged with its type and row count and shares the 15-per-minute download limit with report downloads (429 after that). Only admins: signed out is redirected, a normal account gets 403 on every type, and the buttons are hidden from it.');
$add('CSV-002', 'Export and import', 'Spreadsheet formula injection', 'pass', 'Cells that start with = + - @ or a tab get a leading apostrophe on export (name, address, city and notes checked). The importer removes exactly that apostrophe again, so a formula-looking name comes back unchanged while a normal leading apostrophe is kept.');
$add('CSV-003', 'Export and import', 'Round trip: export, delete, import', 'pass', 'Exporting companies, deleting six of them and importing the whole file re-adds exactly those six field for field and skips every other row as a duplicate; importing the same file again adds nothing. The same for a user, including role, status, country, company, job title and phone.');
$add('CSV-004', 'Export and import', 'Malformed, hostile and oversized files', 'pass', 'Refused with a clear message: no file, wrong or double extension, empty file, header only, missing required column (lists the columns found), binary content, invalid UTF-8, more than 1000 rows, over 200 KB. A 300 KB upload is stopped by Apache (413) before PHP. A wrong CSRF token is 403. None of them created a record. The file is only read from PHP temporary copy: import.php never moves, stores or includes it.');
$add('CSV-005', 'Export and import', 'Good rows are kept, bad rows are explained', 'pass', 'A mixed semicolon file with a BOM, blank line, quoted line breaks and ragged rows: 3 added, 2 duplicates skipped (same KvK number or email, never overwritten), 5 rejected, each listed with its line number and reason. Users: invalid role, status, email, unknown company and empty name are rejected; a duplicate email is skipped. Everything in one transaction; the import is logged with its counts.');
$add('CSV-006', 'Export and import', 'Test suite and shared includes', 'fixed', 'Loading the new CSV include next to invoices.php made PHP stop with "Cannot redeclare money()" in the test run, because the same file was loaded by two different paths.', 'csv.php now loads its helpers only when their functions are not defined yet; the test no longer requires invoices.php itself.');


// ---------- Stage 6: notifications
$add('NOTIF-001', 'Notifications', 'The four events', 'pass', 'A refresh records one notification each for: an invoice that became overdue (with the amount owed and a link), a backup that failed in the last 48 hours, a monitored service that is down (endpoint checks, and Uptime Kuma monitors that changed to down in the last day) and an open urgent ticket. Healthy or switched-off endpoints, old failures, completed backups, normal or resolved tickets and non-status-change heartbeats create nothing.');
$add('NOTIF-002', 'Notifications', 'No duplicates', 'pass', 'Each notification has a unique key made from the event itself (for example invoice-overdue:12). More refreshes announce nothing again and the database refuses the same key twice. A second outage of the same endpoint, after it recovered, is a new event and is announced once. Resolving a ticket keeps its earlier notification.');
$add('NOTIF-003', 'Notifications', 'Refresh runs when pages load, at most every three minutes', 'pass', 'The slot is claimed with one atomic UPDATE, so two simultaneous page loads do not both run the checks. Inside the window nothing runs; after it, the next page load runs them once and the following load does not. A failure in this code is logged and never stops a page from loading. Notifications older than 90 days are removed.');
$add('NOTIF-004', 'Notifications', 'Bell, dropdown and notifications page', 'pass', 'The top bar has a bell with the unread count (also in its text label), a dropdown with the latest six, Mark all read and a link to notifications.php (all / unread, mark one read, mark all read, pagination, friendly empty states). Marking needs a CSRF token; the return address after Mark all read only accepts a local page name. Notification text is escaped everywhere. Seen in the browser at 1440 px.');
$add('NOTIF-005', 'Notifications', 'Reduced motion', 'pass', 'The bell only rings (twice, then stops) inside a prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference media query, and it is a native details element, so it works with the keyboard and without JavaScript; Escape and an outside click close it.');
$add('NOTIF-006', 'Notifications', 'Notification email address in Settings', 'pass', 'Settings > Account (admins only) has the address, pre-filled with denis@telecomlijn.nl from the database seed and the code default. Invalid addresses are refused, a normal account does not see the field and gets 403 on a forged save, an empty value turns emails off. Sending itself is built in stage 8; notifications already carry an emailed_at column for it.');
$add('NOTIF-007', 'Notifications', 'Demo data', 'pass', 'Notifications about demo invoices, backups and tickets are tagged as demo and are removed with the demo data.');


// ---------- Stage 7: two-factor sign-in
$add('2FA-001', 'Two-factor', 'Algorithm against the official test values', 'pass', 'The code generator is written without outside libraries (HMAC-SHA1, 6 digits, 30 seconds). It reproduces all six RFC 6238 test values (8 digits, T = 59 up to 20000000000), the ten RFC 4226 counter values and the known base32 form of the RFC secret. Previous and next 30-second codes are accepted for clock differences; older, later, short, long or non-numeric codes are refused; spaces typed in a code are ignored.');
$add('2FA-002', 'Two-factor', 'Turning it on from Settings > Account', 'pass', 'Set-up shows a random 160-bit key to type into an authenticator app (grouped in fours) and an otpauth link; there is no QR code because that needs a library. Nothing is switched on until the first code is confirmed (a wrong or malformed code changes nothing). Then ten recovery codes are shown once; a reload no longer shows them. The secret is stored encrypted, the recovery codes only as 64-character keyed hashes, and the set-up secret never leaves the signed-in session.');
$add('2FA-003', 'Two-factor', 'Sign-in with the code step', 'pass', 'With two-step on, the right password leads to login_2fa.php and nobody is signed in until the code is accepted: the dashboard and settings stay closed, and the code page is unreachable without passing the password step. Wrong, expired and made-up codes are refused. A code step can be used only once: the code that confirmed the set-up, a replay of a code already used for sign-in and anything older than the last used step are all refused. Accounts without two-step (admin / admin) sign in with the password alone, exactly as before.');
$add('2FA-004', 'Two-factor', 'Recovery codes', 'pass', 'A recovery code (any capitals, with or without the dash) signs in once and is then used up; the page counts the remaining ones; the sign-in is logged as a warning. It also works as proof when turning two-step off.');
$add('2FA-005', 'Two-factor', 'Lock-out', 'pass', 'Wrong codes count per address in the same table as password failures: five are answered with an error, the sixth attempt is locked out even with a correct code and the login page explains why. A turned-off request on the Account page is subject to the same lock. Every wrong code is in the activity log.');
$add('2FA-006', 'Two-factor', 'Turning it off and admin reset', 'pass', 'Turning off needs the account password and a valid code (or recovery code); a wrong password, wrong code or no code changes nothing; it erases the secret and recovery codes and is logged. An admin can reset another person from Settings > Team (secret and recovery codes erased, logged); a normal account gets 403 on a forged reset, and resetting yourself from Team is refused. After a reset the person signs in with the password and can set it up again.');


// ---------- Stage 8: email, password reset, invitations
$add('MAIL-001', 'Email', 'Mailer and Settings > Email', 'pass', 'Every message is written to the outbox first, then sent through the SMTP server entered in Settings > Email (own small SMTP client: login, STARTTLS or SSL, dot-stuffing). Tested against a mock SMTP server: login, sender and recipient arrive correctly, the subject is encoded for accents, the body is base64 UTF-8; a refused login, a refused recipient and a closed port are reported as failed without the password in the message. The password is stored encrypted, never shown (only "saved"), kept when the field is left empty and logged without its value. Without settings on localhost messages stay in the outbox, where an admin reads them and copies a link.');
$add('MAIL-002', 'Email', 'Header injection and one-time links in the outbox', 'pass', 'A recipient with a line break, a nonsense or over-long address is refused before anything is sent; a line break in the subject or sender name cannot add a header. The outbox shows messages as escaped text. A delivered message that contained a one-time link loses its text; entries older than 30 days are removed. Normal accounts get 403 on the tab and on forged save or clear requests.');
$add('MAIL-003', 'Email', 'Notification emails (finishing stage 6)', 'pass', 'New notifications are emailed to the address in Settings > Account: one email per refresh (a single event names the event, several are one digest) with links to the items. The same event is never mailed twice, an emptied address sends nothing and the backlog is not mailed later, and demo-data events are never mailed to the real address. Links need a site address (see MAIL-005).');
$add('RESET-001', 'Password reset', 'Request: nothing revealed, limits', 'pass', '"Forgot password?" on the login page opens forgot.php. A real account, an unknown one and a disabled one get a page that is character for character the same; only a real account gets an email and a reset record. A reset without a CSRF token is 403, one account can have at most 3 requests per hour (more are ignored silently) and requests are limited to 5 a minute per address.');
$add('RESET-002', 'Password reset', 'Token and password change', 'pass', 'The token is 64 random hex characters; only its SHA-256 hash is stored; valid for one hour; usable once (claimed atomically). Tampered, truncated, reversed, upper-cased, extended and SQL-looking tokens, expired and used links all show "This link does not work". The new password needs 12 to 256 characters, a matching confirmation and must not contain the user name; refused attempts leave the link usable. After a reset the old password stops working and every session that was open before it ends (a session epoch on the account), while a new sign-in works. The request and the completed reset are in the activity log.');
$add('RESET-003', 'Password reset', 'Link address can not be forged', 'pass', 'Links in emails use the site address saved in Settings > Email. With none saved on a real server no address is guessed from the request (a forged Host header gets nothing and the reset is not sent, which is logged); only on localhost the request address is used. The .htaccess already redirects other host names to https.');
$add('INVITE-001', 'Invitations', 'Invite by email from Settings > Team', 'pass', 'An admin enters name, username, email, role and integrations access; the person gets a link (valid 3 days, usable once, only the hash stored). A new invitation for the same person replaces the old one; pending invitations can be withdrawn; used, expired, withdrawn and tampered links show "This invitation does not work". Normal accounts get 403 on forged invites and withdrawals.');
$add('INVITE-002', 'Invitations', 'Accepting an invitation', 'pass', 'The person chooses a password (same rules as above) and gets an account with the invited role and permission (an invited admin gets full integrations access), no forced password change, is signed in and lands on Settings > Account where two-step sign-in can be turned on. If the username was taken in the meantime, no second account is created. Markup in an invited name is escaped. Guessing at invitation links is rate limited (429).');
$add('MAIL-004', 'Email', 'Not tested against a real mail server', 'open', 'Everything was tested against a mock SMTP server on localhost without TLS. STARTTLS / SSL against a real provider, and the PHP mail() path on a real server, have not been exercised. Also, a reset request for a real account takes slightly longer than for an unknown one (it sends the email), so a very patient attacker could in theory tell them apart by timing; the page itself is identical.', 'Enter real SMTP details in Settings > Email and use "Send a test email". Moving the sending to a background queue would remove the timing difference.');
$add('MAIL-005', 'Email', 'Fill in later: SMTP account and site address', 'info', 'Settings > Email is left blank on purpose. Until an SMTP account and the site address (for example https://admin.telecomlijn.nl) are entered, nothing is delivered: reset and invitation links appear in the outbox and, on a real server, reset emails are not sent at all.');


// ---------- Stage 9: trends on the Overview
$add('TREND-001', 'Trends', 'Four charts on the Overview, numbers checked in a clean database', 'pass', 'Revenue per month (payments, last 12 months), new users per month, tickets opened per week and average time to resolve (by the week a ticket was resolved), all plain HTML bars like the activity chart, no chart library. A scratch database built from the real schema with known rows gave exact results: payments summed per month with older ones left out, users counted by creation month, ticket volume per ISO week, and the open-time average (17 h, 24 h and a ticket opened five weeks earlier counted in the week it was resolved). Week keys equal MySQL YEARWEEK mode 3, including across New Year; live totals equal direct SUM/COUNT queries.');
$add('TREND-002', 'Trends', 'Empty state', 'pass', 'With no data each series still covers its whole range (0 per period, and null rather than 0 hours when nothing was resolved) and all four charts show a "No data yet" box instead of empty bars.');
$add('TREND-003', 'Trends', 'Hover, keyboard and screen readers', 'pass', 'Every bar carries its value as data-tip (the existing cursor-following tooltip shows it on hover), the same text as aria-label, and is focusable so the value shows on keyboard focus. Each chart has a text description with total and peak, and a "View as table" fallback with caption and row/column headers; missing values show as a dash. Labels and values are escaped.');
$add('TREND-004', 'Trends', 'Layout bug found in the browser', 'fixed', 'The first version placed the charts inside the yellow status box (the insertion matched the Demo data button first). After moving it the bars were invisible because the new class name .tip collided with the existing tooltip class, which is position:fixed and starts transparent.', 'Charts now sit between the activity chart and the demo-data panel and use their own .vbar class; the tooltip system from motion.js is reused for hover.');
$add('TREND-005', 'Trends', 'Demo data history', 'pass', 'Demo data now adds 70 older invoices, all paid in full, spread over the last 12 months (tagged as demo and removed with it); users already spanned 14 months and tickets are limited to 12 weeks, so every chart has something to show.');


// ---------- Stage 10: PDF invoices and recurring invoices
$add('PDF-001', 'PDF invoices', 'Our own PDF writer', 'pass', 'includes/pdf.php writes A4 PDFs with the built-in Helvetica fonts, no library. Tests check the structure (header, trailer, every cross-reference offset pointing at its object, every stream declaring its exact length, page count), escaping of parentheses and backslashes, Windows-1252 conversion (euro sign, accents) and text widths from the Helvetica tables. The output was also read back with pdftotext: text, euro signs and table layout come out as intended.');
$add('PDF-002', 'PDF invoices', 'Invoice PDF contents and download', 'pass', 'invoice_pdf.php?id= gives an attachment named invoice-NUMBER.pdf (not cached, correct Content-Length) with the supplier, customer and address, dates, BTW rate, every line (long descriptions wrap, 70 lines continue over numbered pages with a repeated header), subtotal, BTW, total, paid, balance due and a payment line; a paid invoice says so. Signed out is redirected, an unknown or non-numeric id is 404, downloads are logged and share the 15-a-minute download limit. Every invoice page has a Download PDF button.');
$add('PDF-003', 'PDF invoices', 'BTW number and IBAN stay off until you enter them', 'pass', 'The made-up placeholder numbers are gone: BTW number and IBAN now start empty, are left off the PDF completely (also from the payment line), and the invoice page shows "not set" with a reminder. Settings > Company details (admins only) takes them; the IBAN is checked with the mod-97 test (valid samples from four countries accepted, altered or malformed ones refused), a Dutch BTW number must look like NL123456789B01. Once saved they appear on the PDF and the invoice page; emptied again they disappear. Text typed there is escaped on the page and plain text in the PDF.');
$add('INV-006', 'Invoices', 'Real BTW number and IBAN (replaces INV-005)', 'info', 'INV-005 said the supplier numbers were placeholders in includes/company.php. They are now entered in Settings > Company details and start empty. You still have to fill in your BTW number and IBAN there before invoices are sent to customers.');
$add('REC-001', 'Recurring invoices', 'Creating invoices from a schedule', 'pass', 'A due schedule creates exactly one invoice per run, dated on the scheduled day, with the normal numbering, billed to the company (name, address, email), one line with the schedule description, due date from its payment terms, BTW rounded correctly (21%, 9%, and 0% with a note giving the reason). The schedule then moves on one month, quarter or year and remembers the last run. Several schedules due at once each get their own invoice. A schedule far behind catches up one invoice per run.');
$add('REC-002', 'Recurring invoices', 'No duplicates', 'pass', 'Running again, running many times, the Run now button, opening the site and the command-line script never create a second invoice for a period. Underneath, a unique key on (schedule, issue date) means the database refuses it, and a schedule wound back to an invoiced date only advances. A run at the same moment as another waits on a named lock; nothing is lost and the schedule is still created exactly once afterwards.');
$add('REC-003', 'Recurring invoices', 'Dates at month ends', 'pass', 'A monthly schedule from 31 January invoices on 28 February (29 in a leap year) and returns to the 31st; quarterly and yearly schedules and the December-to-January rollover are right; a schedule from 29 February goes to 28 February in a normal year.');
$add('REC-004', 'Recurring invoices', 'Pause, resume, delete, run automatically', 'pass', 'A paused schedule creates nothing even when its date has passed; resuming moves the next date to today or later, so paused months are not billed afterwards. Delete asks for confirmation and keeps the invoices already made. Due schedules are created automatically when the site is opened (with the notification refresh, at most every three minutes) and by run_recurring.php for a scheduled task (not startable from the web). The new-schedule form validates every field and escapes its text.');
$add('REC-005', 'Recurring invoices', 'Demo data', 'pass', 'Demo data adds four schedules (one paused) with all next dates in the future, so loading it never creates invoices by itself; they are removed with the demo data.');
$add('TEST-006', 'Test log', 'Test suite fixes while building stage 10', 'fixed', 'The old-database migration test could not drop companies once recurring invoices pointed at it; a test of an invoice note wrote a SQL backslash wrongly; a test reused today as the date of a schedule that had already been invoiced for today (correctly treated as a duplicate); and a wrapping test split text on a literal backslash-n.', 'The test now drops the newer tables first, escapes the backslash, uses a fresh date per trigger and splits on a real newline.');

return ['version' => 17, 'entries' => $e];
